.TH STRDUP 3 "May 27, 2026"
.UC 7
.SH NAME
\fBstrdup\fP \- save a copy of a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <string.h>
.sp
.B char *
.br
\fBstrdup\fP(\fIconst char *s\fP)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR strdup ()
function
allocates sufficient memory for a copy of the string \fIs\fP, does the copy
and returns a pointer to the allocated memory.  The pointer may be used as
an argument to free(3).
.SH RETURN VALUES
The
.BR strdup ()
function
returns NULL and sets \fBerrno\fP to ENOMEM if insufficient memory is available.
.SH SEE ALSO
malloc(3),
bcopy(3)
.SH HISTORY
The
.BR strdup ()
function
first appeared in 4.4BSD
